description:
Implement `useDragDrop` to manage drag-and-drop reordering of a list. It returns the current item order, event handlers to attach to each item, and the index of the item currently being dragged.

**Example:**
```tsx
function SortableList() {
  const { items, onDragStart, onDragOver, onDrop, draggingIndex } = useDragDrop(['A', 'B', 'C']);

  return (
    <ul>
      {items.map((item, i) => (
        <li
          key={item}
          draggable
          onDragStart={() => onDragStart(i)}
          onDragOver={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); onDragOver(i); }}
          onDrop={() => onDrop(i)}
          style={{ opacity: draggingIndex === i ? 0.5 : 1 }}
        >
          {item}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

